  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The works to which this consent relates, must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of this consent.\r\n\r\nReason: To accord with the provisions of Section 18(1) of the Planning (Listed Buildings and Conservation areas) Act 1990.",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and specifications: [190923-1000, 190923- 1050, 190923-1403, 190923-1501, 190923-1054, TS084-1-GA-02 00, TS084-1-GA-03 00, Archaeological Desk Based Assessment [dated November 2019], Air Quality Assessment [dated December 2022], Biodiversity Net Gain Assessment [dated December 2022], Design and Access Statement [dated December 2022], Flood Risk Assessment and Drainage Strategy [dated December 2022], Noise Impact Assessment, Transport Assessment [dated December 2022], Heritage Statement [dated December 2022], Outline Fire Safety Strategy [dated 14 December 2022], Preliminary Ecological Appraisal [dated December 2022], Planning Statement, HUDU Rapid Health Impact Assessment Matrix, Statement of Community Involvement [December 2022] and Technical Note [dated 14 December 2022]. Received 11 January 2023; Energy Statement and Overheating Analysis. Received 23 January 2023; Interior Daylight Analysis. Received 1 February 2023; Noise Impact Assessment. Received 15 March 2023; 190923-1307 P01, 190923-1401 P01 and 190923-1404 P01. Received 21 March 2023; Arboricultural Impact Assessment & Method Statement [dated April 2023]. Received 9 May 2023; Air Quality Assessment Addendum. Received 5 June 2023; 190923-1304 P02, 190923-1305 P02, 190923- 1306 P02, 190923-1052 P02, Rapid Health Impact Assessment Response [dated 8 June 2023] and Staines Road 3D Context Elevations. Received 13 June 2023; 190923-1055 P01, 190923-1402 P02 and 190923-1502 P02. Received 15 June 2023].\r\n\r\nReason: In order to ensure the development is carried out in accordance with the planning permission.",
    "Condition : 3 - Method Statement\r\n\r\nPrior to the commencement of any demolition works to the ancillary kitchen block link attached to the listed building; findings of initial exploration works detailed within the submitted Method Statement, shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. B) Where the findings required by Part A of this condition recommend or necessitate an updated Method Statement, this shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority prior to any demolition works carried out to the single storey link structure.\r\n\r\nReason: To ensure that the development protects the built fabric and the significance of the adjoining Grade II listed building.",
    "Condition : 4 - Prior to the commencement of any demolition works to the ancillary kitchen block linked to the attached listed building, full details of any 'making good' exposed areas of the listed building revealed by demolitions are to be submitted and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority.\r\n\r\nReason: In order to safeguard the architectural and historic interest of the listed building."
  ],
